Third-party code
----------------
None. This port bundles no third-party libraries and no code from any other
port. The only nested jar is the Create Fly Recipe Viewer, a separate MIT mod
by the same porter. The registration helper classes under
net/davio/aquaticambitions/registrate are original work written for this
workspace; their public API names deliberately mirror Registrate's so that
upstream call sites port unchanged, but no Registrate code is included.

Assets
------
Textures, models, structures, translations and data files are the upstream
project's own work and ship under its MIT licence. Minecraft's own textures
(the conduit and its wind animation, the effect icons) are not bundled: the mod
draws them from the game's resources at runtime. Assets belonging to Create Fly
are not bundled either; the mod resolves them from Create Fly at runtime.
